# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the sliced host-tier restore window (docs/prefix-store-hygiene.md "Sliced restore"; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the branch that carries the sliced restore and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed head that carries the sliced restore (tp4/tier-slice, or the ship-4 branch after the integrator merged it;
# sed -i 's/tp4-ship-4/<tag>/' *.env). The flag lives in files the image carries (qwen_prefix_registry.py, qwen_prefix_scheduler_patch.py, serving_prefill_admission.py): an image built before it ignores the two names and
# the arm reads NOT_EXERCISED (no "host tier restore slice on" line). This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# Z: the window's end: status and an all-four reset, no agent start (the cards stay under development). The owner restores the ARC runner sets to their normal scale, then production: card
# reset, link measurement, topology republish, agent restart, deploy and the post-checks. Duration (estimate): 10 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4
